  "user_request_original": "Design a 21-layer Ta2O5/SiO2 defect-cavity bandpass filter on fused silica substrate with air incident medium. Layer sequence: alternating Ta2O5/SiO2 starting with Ta2O5, layer 11 is the defect cavity. Initialize all layers within ±10% of quarter-wave thickness at 1550 nm (Ta2O5 ~185 nm, SiO2 ~267 nm, cavity ~534 nm). Constrain chirp slope to maximum 3% thickness change per interface. Use CMA-ES optimizer with population size 20, seeded with thickness vector [209.8257105224059, 220.79821841120258, 214.56223999475006, 185.44557829172606, 226.69413733242868, 233.2332709326123, 96.19862533257114, 95.2239899876587, 184.9256993446736, 183.53306613797727, 337.39530803995683, 211.76520107676225, 165.31201322409683, 178.26505740914925, 274.47316942425505, 142.75439461585967, 241.4702554145756, 365.64105969518573, 377.85960538578905, 349.3859455073734, 303.5795815352078]. Evaluate transmittance at normal incidence for wavelengths 1400-1700 nm. Optimize for high transmittance at 1550 nm and low transmittance in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm bands. Topology realization override: disregard any symbolic repeat count, range, or ellipsis above and use exactly 5 alternating Ta2O5/SiO2 pairs, one cavity layer, and exactly 5 reverse-order pairs (21 finite layers). Optimize only continuous physical thicknesses; the task compiler must fully expand every finite layer. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 1400-1500 nm, 1550-1550 nm, 1600-1700 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance at 1550 nm (soft target ≥ 0.95); strong suppression of transmittance in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 1400-1500 nm; transmittance in 1600-1700 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layers ≤ 30.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Design a 21-layer Ta2O5/SiO2 bandpass filter on fused silica with air incidence. Sequence: five alternating Ta2O5/SiO2 pairs, a central Ta2O5 defect cavity (layer 11), followed by five reverse-order SiO2/Ta2O5 pairs. Initialize thicknesses using the provided seed vector. Optimize continuous thicknesses over 1400–1700 nm at normal incidence to maximize transmission at 1550 nm while suppressing transmission in 1400–1500 nm and 1600–1700 nm bands. Apply ±10% relative manufacturing tolerance.",
